2. Closed-source capability  --  NOT covered by the GPLv3 grant
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The generative-AI capability (the "Generative_AI_Service") is a closed-source,
hosted service that is account-gated and requires a valid authenticated user
account (an active subscription entitlement or valid Bring-Your-Own-Key
credentials) before access is granted (see Requirements 6, 9, and 13.2).

  * The Generative_AI_Service backend, its models, and its server-side source
    code are proprietary and are NOT distributed under the GPLv3 and are NOT
    part of the Corresponding Source of the open-source components above.

  * This repository contains only the open-source GPLv3 CLIENT code that talks
    to the hosted Generative_AI_Service over the network. The client stub is
    GPLv3; the remote service it contacts is not.

  * When no network connection or authenticated account is available, the
    open-source editor, MCP server, and agent chat continue to function; only
    the generative capability is unavailable, and the application surfaces a
    non-blocking indication to that effect (see Requirement 13.4).

